cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "VAERS 1990–2026, searchable: a PII-free structured derivative of the U.S. Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System"
abstract: >-
  A clean, structured, privacy-preserving derivative of the U.S. VAERS
  dataset (1990–2026), organized in a uniform 69-column who/what/when/where/how
  format. Built only from structured coded fields (no free-text), with the
  derivation method, sample data, pre-pulled query results, and verification
  path included. Hypothesis-generating signal-detection data, not
  hypothesis-testing; counts are a floor and carry no denominator.
authors:
  - alias: meridian-north
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-31"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - VAERS
  - pharmacovigilance
  - vaccine safety
  - adverse events
  - open data
  - reproducible research
repository-code: "https://github.com/meridian-north/vaers-1990-2026-searchable"
type: dataset
references:
  - type: data
    title: "VAERS — Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (source data)"
    authors:
      - name: "U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention / Food and Drug Administration"
    url: "https://vaers.hhs.gov/data/datasets.html"
    notes: "Public-domain source. This dataset is a structured derivative."
